  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 1
    m_Localized: Tutorial
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2
    m_Localized: Close
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3
    m_Localized: Skip all tutorials
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4
    m_Localized: How Combat Works
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5
    m_Localized: Combat is automatic. Your character and enemies attack on their own.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6
    m_Localized: Each unit has a health bar and an attack bar. When the attack bar
      is full, the unit attacks. Then the bar starts filling again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7
    m_Localized: Choose Your Class
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8
    m_Localized: Your character grows through the skill tree. Each point you spend
      unlocks new strengths and shapes your build.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9
    m_Localized: You have your first skill point! Left-click a class node in the
      skill tree to choose your class.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10
    m_Localized: Leveling Up
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11
    m_Localized: Defeat enemies to earn experience. When you have enough, you level
      up and get skill points.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12
    m_Localized: Use these points in the skill tree. You can explore any branch
      and choose the skills you want.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13
    m_Localized: Damage Types
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 14
    m_Localized: One attack can deal several types of damage at once. Physical damage
      is the most common type.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15
    m_Localized: Armor and barrier protect you from physical damage.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 16
    m_Localized: Attacks can also deal elemental damage. Fire, cold and lightning
      are the three elemental damage types.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17
    m_Localized: Resistances reduce elemental damage. Elemental resistance applies
      to all three elements and stacks multiplicatively with each element's own resistance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18
    m_Localized: 'Ailments'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19
    m_Localized: 'Ailments are harmful effects that attacks can apply. They can deal damage over time or weaken the target.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 20
    m_Localized: 'Dealing damage always gives you a chance to apply the matching ailment. This chance depends on how much damage of that type the attack deals.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 21
    m_Localized: 'The base chance is the share of the target''s maximum health that this damage represents. A bigger share means a higher chance.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22
    m_Localized: "Physical - Bleed\nFire - Ignite\nCold - Chill\nLightning - Overcharge"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 23
    m_Localized: "World Map"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 24
    m_Localized: "The first boss is defeated! This is the world map, where you choose where to go next."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25
    m_Localized: "Click a location to view its information, stages, and rewards. Choose an available location and enter when you are ready for battle."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 26
    m_Localized: "The farther a location is from the start of your journey, the stronger its enemies and the greater its rewards. Move forward, strengthen your hero, and unlock new locations!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
